[{:db/id 17592186064307 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b4ed5979-35bd-5227-b6d2-7a9f08a0cbdf" "question-31fc854a-70c5-5387-9f4b-327eb3d213ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4ed5979-35bd-5227-b6d2-7a9f08a0cbdf" :question/id #uuid "b4ed5979-35bd-5227-b6d2-7a9f08a0cbdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-138812" :question/problem "Consider the function $y=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}.$ Its derivative is given by \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))+(x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-67f1cc61-ae77-5747-982e-80a1c789aa8a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-67f1cc61-ae77-5747-982e-80a1c789aa8a" :answer-field/id #uuid "67f1cc61-ae77-5747-982e-80a1c789aa8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a22eeb7f-6011-5b02-bcc9-4fb5207df252" :answer-field/choices ["answer-07b2dd31-87ef-57c3-a041-f20e700d80c6" "answer-21ede1b3-ec6b-56c3-a5bd-57ae68918058" "answer-13f20f22-f41f-5f1b-8d9d-f2adb8019550" "answer-a22eeb7f-6011-5b02-bcc9-4fb5207df252" "answer-f63be48c-a2c8-558a-af22-1c2d536b7b18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07b2dd31-87ef-57c3-a041-f20e700d80c6" :answer/id #uuid "07b2dd31-87ef-57c3-a041-f20e700d80c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21ede1b3-ec6b-56c3-a5bd-57ae68918058" :answer/id #uuid "21ede1b3-ec6b-56c3-a5bd-57ae68918058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13f20f22-f41f-5f1b-8d9d-f2adb8019550" :answer/id #uuid "13f20f22-f41f-5f1b-8d9d-f2adb8019550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a22eeb7f-6011-5b02-bcc9-4fb5207df252" :answer/id #uuid "a22eeb7f-6011-5b02-bcc9-4fb5207df252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f63be48c-a2c8-558a-af22-1c2d536b7b18" :answer/id #uuid "f63be48c-a2c8-558a-af22-1c2d536b7b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064308 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5a381386-3c00-511f-88a6-9a57fbf09d3b" "question-6d2d4364-ca99-526d-979f-b7f7eb9eac46" "question-fed635cb-d378-5d78-b478-1026e862dee7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5a381386-3c00-511f-88a6-9a57fbf09d3b" :question/id #uuid "5a381386-3c00-511f-88a6-9a57fbf09d3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-138855" :question/problem "Consider the function $y=(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Its derivative is given by \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x))+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡x) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-795f926a-e3fd-544a-ba60-66f3eb632b18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-795f926a-e3fd-544a-ba60-66f3eb632b18" :answer-field/id #uuid "795f926a-e3fd-544a-ba60-66f3eb632b18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-228d9dea-2b4e-5f17-8cd2-d73751d80342" :answer-field/choices ["answer-228d9dea-2b4e-5f17-8cd2-d73751d80342" "answer-602de7c1-ef38-5158-8b6f-d070c0442d32" "answer-e984a0af-51e1-5904-82b6-34c5f776d3f8" "answer-e31a12e8-2630-53d1-8e4f-075fa6dd173e" "answer-df0b2f5d-7c7c-5292-bd94-2ac5f79bd226"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-228d9dea-2b4e-5f17-8cd2-d73751d80342" :answer/id #uuid "228d9dea-2b4e-5f17-8cd2-d73751d80342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{cot}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-602de7c1-ef38-5158-8b6f-d070c0442d32" :answer/id #uuid "602de7c1-ef38-5158-8b6f-d070c0442d32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e984a0af-51e1-5904-82b6-34c5f776d3f8" :answer/id #uuid "e984a0af-51e1-5904-82b6-34c5f776d3f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e31a12e8-2630-53d1-8e4f-075fa6dd173e" :answer/id #uuid "e31a12e8-2630-53d1-8e4f-075fa6dd173e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df0b2f5d-7c7c-5292-bd94-2ac5f79bd226" :answer/id #uuid "df0b2f5d-7c7c-5292-bd94-2ac5f79bd226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-31fc854a-70c5-5387-9f4b-327eb3d213ff" :question/id #uuid "31fc854a-70c5-5387-9f4b-327eb3d213ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-341727" :question/problem "Given that $y=(2x+3)^{x}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(2x+3)^{x-1}\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(2x+3)^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((2x+3)^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3))+(x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)+x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2x+3}\\cdot 2) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)+\\frac{2x}{2x+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)+\\frac{2x}{2x+3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(2x+3)^{x}:$    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+3)^{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)+\\frac{2x}{2x+3}) \\\\  & =(2x+3)^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{(2x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)}{2x+3}+\\frac{2x}{2x+3}) \\\\  & =(2x+3)^{x-1}\\cdot ((2x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+3)+2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d44a882d-c0e6-5d33-a2fe-067332daaf5d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d44a882d-c0e6-5d33-a2fe-067332daaf5d" :answer-field/id #uuid "d44a882d-c0e6-5d33-a2fe-067332daaf5d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-28bc056c-eb5f-5687-8409-0974c7956f17" :answer-field/choices ["answer-28bc056c-eb5f-5687-8409-0974c7956f17"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28bc056c-eb5f-5687-8409-0974c7956f17" :answer/id #uuid "28bc056c-eb5f-5687-8409-0974c7956f17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2x+3)\\ln(2x+3)+2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d2d4364-ca99-526d-979f-b7f7eb9eac46" :question/id #uuid "6d2d4364-ca99-526d-979f-b7f7eb9eac46" :question/math-academy-id "q-341945" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y={(\\sqrt{2x+1})}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ at $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$ equals the function's derivative at the corresponding point.\n\nWe have the function \n\n$$\ny={(\\sqrt{2x+1})}^{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({(\\sqrt{2x+1})}^{{x}^{2}+1}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{2x+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{2x+1})) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,{y}^{′} & =({x}^{2}+1)^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{2x+1})+({x}^{2}+1)\\,{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{2x+1}))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,{y}^{′} & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{2x+1})+({x}^{2}+1)\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}\\cdot \\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{2x+1}}) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\,(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2x+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y={(\\sqrt{2x+1})}^{{x}^{2}+1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={(\\sqrt{2x+1})}^{{x}^{2}+1}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2x+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y={(\\sqrt{2x+1})}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={y}^{′}{|}_{x=0} & ={(\\sqrt{2(0)+1})}^{(0)^{2}+1}(0\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2(0)+1)+\\frac{(0)^{2}+1}{2(0)+1}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (0\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76f8ee9f-a89b-56b6-9a08-fe333af36907"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76f8ee9f-a89b-56b6-9a08-fe333af36907" :answer-field/id #uuid "76f8ee9f-a89b-56b6-9a08-fe333af36907" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e24a86b9-7405-5dbf-acfb-1af04c6cd34f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e24a86b9-7405-5dbf-acfb-1af04c6cd34f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e24a86b9-7405-5dbf-acfb-1af04c6cd34f" :answer/id #uuid "e24a86b9-7405-5dbf-acfb-1af04c6cd34f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fed635cb-d378-5d78-b478-1026e862dee7" :question/id #uuid "fed635cb-d378-5d78-b478-1026e862dee7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341953" :question/problem "Given that $y=(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}$, find ${y}^{′}.$\n\n${y}^{′}=-(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\,+$\n\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)))+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(x))) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{csc}^{2}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,(\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)})}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)})} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-33b8438b-3327-575c-ae05-92d222d1ed04"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-33b8438b-3327-575c-ae05-92d222d1ed04" :answer-field/id #uuid "33b8438b-3327-575c-ae05-92d222d1ed04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-96beea54-57c3-53ca-9a62-26604472224a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96beea54-57c3-53ca-9a62-26604472224a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96beea54-57c3-53ca-9a62-26604472224a" :answer/id #uuid "96beea54-57c3-53ca-9a62-26604472224a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\csc(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-8ddfa349-33f9-52db-ae99-fde6c1886942" :activity/id #uuid "8ddfa349-33f9-52db-ae99-fde6c1886942" :activity/title "Logarithmic Differentiation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048773 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-2312e57b-a556-5b41-9d0e-0eea036d1a63" "step-dc6